  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div id=\"\"> <p>APOD</p> <p>Astronomy Picture of the Day</p> <p> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer. </p> <div><p><img width=\"5815\" height=\"4976\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=5815&amp;h=4976&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"A pair of snow topped volcanoes are seen in the distance. A background starry sky is seen behind them, with a red filamentary nebula looping around that appears to connect the two tops of the volcanoes.\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=5815&amp;h=4976&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 5815w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=300&amp;h=257&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=768&amp;h=657&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=876&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=1314&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=2048&amp;h=1753&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2048w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=400&amp;h=342&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=600&amp;h=513&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=900&amp;h=770&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=1027&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_5815.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1711&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 5815px) 100vw, 5815px\"><img width=\"960\" height=\"821\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=960&amp;h=821&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" alt=\"A pair of snow topped volcanoes are seen in the distance. A background starry sky is seen behind them, with a red filamentary nebula looping around that appears to connect the two tops of the volcanoes.\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=960&amp;h=821&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 960w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=300&amp;h=257&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=768&amp;h=657&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=400&amp;h=342&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=600&amp;h=513&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/july/LoopVolcanos_Laserna_960_annotated.jpg?w=900&amp;h=770&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"></p></div> <div> <p><strong>Explanation:&nbsp;</strong>What's connecting these two volcanoes? In ancient folklore, the two volcanoes,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/Jwpue5dq_wA?t=171\">Parinacota (left) and Pomerape (right)</a>, are connected by representing a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://qhapaqnan.qiri.cl/ancient-legends/\">mythical</a>&nbsp;prince and princess who engaged in a forbidden romance. Beneath the ground, the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/parinacota-volcano-south-america-76144/\">two peaks</a>&nbsp;are not known to be connected by a common pool of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap051002.html\">hot magma</a>, and neither volcano has erupted in the past 1000 years. Above the ground, there is usually nothing in the sky that connects them -- except if you use careful timing and look from a specific location. The&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DXpszcJCY6n/\">featured well-planned image</a>&nbsp;was captured from&nbsp;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolivia\">Bolivia</a>&nbsp;in mid-April with a series of camera exposures taken on the same day and from the same location. Then,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap090224.html\">Barnard's Loop</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fi.redd.it%2F56kpgyhj47dg1.png\">appeared</a>&nbsp;to connect the volcanic peaks. Also visible in the image is the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/fap/ap260218.html\">Orion Nebula</a>&nbsp;in the center, the star&nbsp;<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/universe/what-is-betelgeuse-inside-the-strange-volatile-star/\">Betelgeuse</a>&nbsp;on the right, and the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap200329.html\">Rosette</a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap250214.html\">Nebula</a>&nbsp;on the upper right.</p><p><strong>Tomorrow's picture:</strong> open space </p></div> </div></div>",
